<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">
	<PropertyGroup>
		<RootNamespace>Assimalign.Cohesion.Web.Rewrite</RootNamespace>
		<Description>URL rewriting and redirect rules for the Cohesion Web pipeline. UseRewrite(rules => ...) evaluates code-first rules in registration order ahead of routing: an internal rewrite hands the rest of the pipeline a request view whose path and query are the rewritten values (IWebRewriteFeature keeps the originals, and inside a Map branch the branch's effective path is rewritten), a redirect answers 301, 302, 307 or 308 with a Location and ends the pipeline, regex rules run interpreted, NonBacktracking or source-generated (never RegexOptions.Compiled), and predicate and delegate rules cover the rest. Canonicalization helpers redirect to HTTPS, to www or non-www, to a trailing slash or none, and to a lowercase path, reading the effective scheme and host a trusted proxy forwarded. Captures are percent-encoded for the part of the URL they land in, rule passes are bounded, and composition is dependency-free and AOT-safe.</Description>
	</PropertyGroup>
	<ItemGroup>
		<CohesionProjectReference Include="Assimalign.Cohesion.Web" />
		<!-- Inside a Map(path) branch the rules see the branch's effective path, and a rewrite
		     publishes a matching IWebPathBaseFeature. Both live in Web.Routing with the branching
		     itself (owner decision 33, #1379). -->
		<CohesionProjectReference Include="Assimalign.Cohesion.Web.Routing" />
		<CohesionProjectReference Include="Assimalign.Cohesion.Http" />
		<CohesionProjectReference Include="Assimalign.Cohesion.Http.Forwarded" />
	</ItemGroup>
</Project>
